1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,800
 that has filled our heart with the true doctrine of Christ,

2
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:07,840
 which has the power to change our language,

3
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:13,480
 and help us speak more as peacemakers today, tomorrow,

4
00:00:13,480 --> 00:00:15,340
 and always.

5
00:00:15,340 --> 00:00:19,440
 As we follow Jesus Christ, we will not only fill his peace,

6
00:00:19,440 --> 00:00:22,480
 but as the Alde Ulysses Chrada said,

7
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:28,080
 we can become an instrument of his peace in the world.

8
00:00:28,080 --> 00:00:32,280
 Let us repent for the harsh language and the expression

9
00:00:32,280 --> 00:00:35,720
 that have offended our friends, leaders,

10
00:00:35,720 --> 00:00:38,760
 or family members, and colleagues.

11
00:00:38,760 --> 00:00:42,800
 Let us pray for peaceful communication among us,

12
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:46,280
 regardless of the difference in our opinions.

13
00:00:46,280 --> 00:00:50,240
 Let us use the language that uplifts, edifies,

14
00:00:50,240 --> 00:00:53,960
 comfort, and brings people together.

15
00:00:53,960 --> 00:00:56,360
 Let us speak with one respect,

16
00:00:56,360 --> 00:01:01,520
 When we speak with each other, let us qualify for its blessings

17
00:01:01,520 --> 00:01:04,920
 by using the language of peacemakers.

18
00:01:04,920 --> 00:01:09,080
 The Savior promised, "Peace I live on with you."

